      "sourceTextSha256": "784eeb8c885dac85f9e54c9c9485c7686f95b1c0be8242cfe83f0ef63c651ad9",
      "text": "Day 9 · After breakfast, a tour of the Brazilian side of the falls. On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, crash into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the torrents boiling into the gorge below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours. Optional: the Macuco Safari or the Bird Park (see Optional excursions).",
      "provenance": {
